{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats","id":578185,"title":"What might be the effects of drinking blood from other major splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-03T22:08:59-07:00","id":578185,"title":"What might be the effects of drinking blood from other major splats?","content":"Werewolves: I think it was mentioned somewhere in 1st edition of Requiem that each success on a feeding roll vs a werewolf gives 2 Vitae, but the werewolf might go into Death Rage. Maybe werewolf blood can also grant temporary Spirit vision if consumed in large quantities or from a powerful werewolf.<br /> <br /> Mages: same yield of Vitae, but might cause extremely vivid hallucinations of Supernal symbols (represented with Conditions like Shaken or Spooked). Clever mages might fool vampires into not feeding from them by saying that Abyssals might mistake a vampire with mage blood inside her for an actual mage (Abyssals won't be fooled, since they can &quot;smell&quot; souls).<br /> <br /> Prometheans: might infuse the vampire with a bit of the humor associated with the promethean's Lineage, leading to mood swings. While the Divine Fire is not literal fire, it can still command its physical version. The Divine Fire might not like the feeling of powering an undead that isn't &quot;meant&quot; to become human. What dangers that might pose to the vampire, I am not sure. Maybe something kinda like a Pandoran happens if said vampire Embraces someone shortly after feeding on a promethean. If the vampire keeps getting in the way of Pilgrimages, the Divine Fire might even send Qashmallim to manipulate events so that said vampire Embraces someone. (The Divine Fire being what it is, another possible scenario is that the vampire might be coerced into messing with Pilgrimages more actively)<br /> <br /> Changelings: I am pretty sure it's mentioned in &quot;Rites Of Springs&quot; that since changeling blood has traces of Glamour, which is associated with dreams and strong emotions, vampires can get really addicted to changeling blood rather quickly. The changeling blood lets them feel truly human for a brief time.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: their blood is fused with lots of Plasm, which might let vampires heal wounds faster at the cost of Ghost vision that can't be turned off for a while. Alternatively, since Plasm is kinda like a conduit for a &quot;Vinculum&quot; between Sin-Eater and Geist, a vampire with Plasm in her blood might get unwanted attention from the Geist which shares that Plasm.<br /> <br /> Mummies: I know very little about this game line, but my hunch is that it tastes horrendous and gives less Vitae. Mummies being time defying corpse-sorcerers and all. It might even leave some vampires very uneasy by giving them small glimpses of Duat when they go into torpor.<br /> <br /> Demons: nothing special if the demon is wearing a Cover, but if taken while she is in demonic form, the vampire might get as sick as a human who just drank motor oil. A particularly sadistic Demon might trick a vampire into making a Pact that forces the vampire to only get Vitae from demonic form blood.<br /> <br /> Beasts: normal Vitae yield but probably tastes...wrong somehow. Might do very weird things to the vampire's body if the blood is taken while the Beast is using an Atavism.<br /> <br /> Man, the Ordo Dracul probably stays up all morning thinking about this stuff.<br /> <br /> What are your ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T22:38:38-07:00","id":578248,"title":"","content":"In first edition they've all been covered, I believe, except for Mummies.<br /> <br /> Werewolves give 2.5 Vitae for each 'normal' Vitae taken, and there's a -2 penalty to resisting frenzy each night per health point taken. I like that one.<br /> <br /> Changeling blood offers a -1 penalty to perception rolls for every Vitae worth consumed, as they get visions similar to low Clarity changelings. Drinking from a fetch offers no Vitae, and the vampire suffers from horrific nightmares during their 'sleep.'<br /> <br /> Prometheans offered half a Vitae for every health point taken, and they understandably taste bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-04-2015, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T22:47:51-07:00","id":578251,"title":"","content":"In 1e, Werewolf blood was worth 2.5 Vitae per &quot;point&quot; worth of blood taken and imposed a -2 penalty to resist Frenzy for a number of nights equal to twice the number of blood points (not Vitae) taken. Mage blood was worth the normal amount of Vitae and caused a Derangement for a number of nights equal to the amount of Vitae taken. Changeling blood was worth the normal amount of Vitae and imposed a -X penalty to perception rolls for one night, where X is the amount of Vitae taken. Promethean blood was worth 1/2 a point of Vitae per &quot;point&quot; of blood taken and had no additional effects. I believe those were the only ones that had &quot;official&quot; special effects in 1e. I've been poking around with updating those to mechanics that fit a bit better with 2e design, and considering adding some effects to the other splats, but I haven't gotten a ton done on it yet. If you like I'll push it up on my conversion to-do list and post the results in a couple days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T22:56:47-07:00","id":578260,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin got the duration of werewolf blood right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:01:09-07:00","id":578261,"title":"","content":"<b>Werewolves:</b> Drinking the blood of a half-flesh, half-spirit hunter of men is a great way to find yourself unconsciously obeying strange folkloric taboos \u2014 much like those followed by the strix.<br /> <b>Mages:</b> Experience something like the Mage Sight \u2014 and become vulnerable to supernal entities whose attentions you suffer.<br /> <b>Prometheans:</b> Another one with a canonical answer from 1e \u2014 Promethean blood tastes thin and unpalatable, and is lacking in Vitae. You have to drink twice as much blood for the same amount of nourishment as from a mortal vessel.<br /> <b>Changelings:</b> Excessive consumption of changeling blood may cause altered states of consciousness and the perceived ability to communicate and bargain with abstract concepts.<br /> <b>Sin-Eaters:</b> You may function as an Anchor for certain ghosts whose attentions you will likely not appreciate. Somehow, in some way, this includes the Sin-Eater's geist, even when the Sin-Eater is still alive and active elsewhere; ambient haunting effects occur, colored by the nature of the geist.<br /> <b>Mummies:</b> Natural animals can sense the uncleanliness of a mummy's remains and reflexively vomit it up if they inadvertantly consume it, but I doubt the Kindred would be deterred. The sahu, the mummy's simulacrum of flesh, is composed of Sekhem, which has associations with life and eternity. As such, their simulated blood probably tastes like a rich banquet, although a vampire drunk on Sekhem might begin to feel the weight of ages.<br /> <b>Demons:</b> Depends on the demon's demonic form. Some may have relatively humanlike blood, while others may taste more like oil or even pressurized air or something. Excessive consumption might confer temporary glitches or temporarily render the vampire a source of aetheric resonance.<br /> <b>Beasts:</b> Outside the Primordial Dream, their blood is human blood. Inside the Primordial Dream, similarly to demons and their demonic forms, it depends on the nature of their Horror. Running on too much Begotten blood might resemble the Red Surrender, making detachment easier but conferring some of the benefits of a frenzy state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:14:53-07:00","id":578297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=578260#post578260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin got the duration of werewolf blood right.</div> </div> </div> </div>People misremember this one all the time because it's just <i>so</i> awkward and fiddly. In my conversion I'm probably just going to make it a straight x2 Vitae to avoid getting into fractional amounts of Vitae, and to make the Vitae gained more consistent with the Duration, of I even put a Duration on it. But I'm leaning more towards just slapping them with the Tempted Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:26:19-07:00","id":578302,"title":"","content":"I think it didn't necessarily needs a definite answer, but some rough guidelines for the Storyteller, so he can create the effect he wishes to such. For two reasons:<br /> <br /> First, with that a ST can choose between runing the game smoothly without paying much heed to what the Kindred player is sucking, or using it to play various themes appropriate to the chronicle. He can even lend different effects depending on particular details about the individual victim and the individual vampire. A Ordo-based chronicle, or at least chapter, as an example, could be entirely based on investigating the effects of exotic blood.<br /> <br /> Second, there will be crossovers. And in them, this becomes a very serious decision, because the most readily available source of blood for a vampire will be another character. I already played such games since cWoD, and I already saw the mess that can create. With a couple of Garou by my side blood become cheaper than apple juice. Of course, most of my Willpower went on resisting frenzy, but since I could spend Blood without stops and even had advantage on doing so (they where both Pure Breed 5, for a juicy +3 Potence &amp; +3 Celerity per turn), it wasn't a problem at all. -2 to resist frenzy will be cheap, very, very cheap, for gaining 2,5 Vitae for a damage that will be healed in 15 minutes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:04:44-07:00","id":578849,"title":"","content":"Personally, I have a very strong dislike of the concept of &quot;drinking supernatural blood is bad for you!&quot; Outside of the WoD, the trope generally amounts to &quot;the stronger the blood, the more powerful you become.&quot; Instead, it becomes &quot;you get effed over.&quot;<br /> <br /> I find that its actually detrimental to play, and encourages games to ignore potential crossover. It kills stories instead of engenders them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:22:25-07:00","id":578919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=578849#post578849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I have a very strong dislike of the concept of &amp;quot;drinking supernatural blood is bad for you!&amp;quot; Outside of the WoD, the trope generally amounts to &amp;quot;the stronger the blood, the more powerful you become.&amp;quot; Instead, it becomes &amp;quot;you get effed over.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I find that its actually detrimental to play, and encourages games to ignore potential crossover. It kills stories instead of engenders them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it necessarily needs to be bad for the vampire. The 1e effects of Werewolf blood, for example, is a mixed blessing any way you look at it. I just like the idea of supernatural creatures' blood having special effects, but those effects dont all need to be bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:04:15-07:00","id":579063,"title":"","content":"Just for fun; the splats I work on.<br /> <br /> Princess: unTransformed - just human blood. Transformed - you feel good and peaceful, but you also gain a form of Sensitivity and feel pain if you hurt others or feed. Before long expect to vomit up the blood as your Beast fights of the hostile and dangerous element.<br /> <br /> Leviathan: Leviathan blood is worth seven times as much as human blood. So long as Leviathan blood is in a Vampire's system she is alive, still a vampire but a living being. The drawback is you're very likely to develop mutations - from cancer to growing tentacles. Best case you mutate some cool new powers, enjoy a few days of life or heal that wound that's been reappearing every time you sleep. Worst case, you turn into a formless mass of mutated flesh. Theophagy isn't for the faint hearted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T13:03:54-07:00","id":579088,"title":"","content":"Given the nature of Sekhem, I'd rule the blood of Mummies as exceptionally potent in Vitae - in fact, so potent the Vampire drinking would actually take damage from it, and potentially feel the full effects of Sybaris flooding through. An addictive and dangerous feast, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T13:28:11-07:00","id":579099,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed, the answer for most of the supernatural types is 'it's just Vitae', I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:19:26-07:00","id":579132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579099#post579099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd ed, the answer for most of the supernatural types is 'it's just Vitae', I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit better than just that though, yes it's just vitae, but functionaly equivalent to vampire vitae for feeding restriction whitout any of the risks of vinculum.<br /> That seems like a good benefit on it's own already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:27:52-07:00","id":579134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579132#post579132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit better than just that though, yes it's just vitae, but functionaly equivalent to vampire vitae for feeding restriction whitout any of the risks of vinculum.<br /> That seems like a good benefit on it's own already.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Unnatural Affinity for this. Interestingly, by RAW it looks like you need a merit to get nourishment at all from other supernaturals in 2e. The first sentence of Unnatural Affinity seems to say such, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:36:57-07:00","id":579142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579134#post579134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need Unnatural Affinity for this. Interestingly, by RAW it looks like you need a merit to get nourishment at all from other supernaturals in 2e. The first sentence of Unnatural Affinity seems to say such, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! That just gave me an idea! What if the weird effects like the Frenzy penalty from werewolf blood and the hallucinations from changeling blood only happen if the vampire doesn't have Unnatural Affinity? Those drawbacks come from not being acclimatized to their unusual vitae, but with the Merit those side effects go away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:05:03-07:00","id":579278,"title":"","content":"I don't say that the effect of supernatural blood have to be detrimental. But that it have to be with a given chronicle needs it to be. If you have an official blessing, then you have an official road to powerplay. Not that powerplay is always a bad thing, mind you. Maybe what your chronicle needs is precisely a way to reasonably turn aside feeding issues, so the vampire PCs can concentrate on other things. Maybe the only effect of Changeling Blood in your game is that such blood can be used as Glamour, and you need that so the vampires can interact more freely with fae and open their own doors to the Hedge. It doesn't matter what supernaturals your group mixes, maybe what you need is precisely that your vampire players have considerable access to boons granted by the blood of their strange friends.<br /> <br /> But another chronicle will be impaired by such. A vampire with seemingly limitless access to blood due to a werewolf companion can become too much powerful for the game. That isn't good if the other players sense they are just fuel to the super-vampire. Also, the drama of your story can be precisely about the difficulties of hunting, and how the mix of characters is something to be handle with caution by the group, for they can be the undoing of one another if not.<br /> <br /> Also, crossover can be handle in a variety of ways, and seriously, I don't think that getting sick with strange blood will be detrimental to that. If you run a game where the players can be of any splat, it isn't the effect of blood that will convince a player to be a vampire, or to be a non-vampire, except maybe on very few cases (and again, with custom effets the ST can handle this in her favor). And if you run a one-splat game but want to add others as NPCs, I heavily doubt you will avoid that just because of detrimental effets of strange blood.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, the strange blood is a sure way to tell vampires that a given person isn't what it seems to be, and from that they are sure to look for more info. Just because as long as they don't know WTH was that, they don't know what kind of dangers or boons they can get. And you don't need boons from the blood, it can even be poisonous. The PCs will search for info even if just to make sure they never get this poison again by accident. By the way, those new guys can have something for them without the need of special blood. Werewolves can offer power over spirits, Chagelings have those juicy Goblin Fruits, and so on.<br /> <br /> Neither the thing about &quot;potent blood&quot; can be so straightforward. It is an element of vampire lore, but being inhuman is also an element of the lore of those creatures. A Demon is a rogue piece of the God-Machine. It makes sence for his blood to be the fluid of a machine, and not blood at all. The Promethean is a being of wild Pyros, the energy of life so badly contained that it turns anathema to life, and also artificial beings to begin with. Changelings are changed by a realm of madness that weren't meant to minds of this plane. Don't forget that the effect of such blood isn't just to highlight the themes of Vampire. More than that, it is to highlight the themes of the victim's template.<br /> <br /> Unnatural Affinity doesn't sound to me as being necessary to feed from such vessels. What that first sentence do is guarantee you will be able to digest such substances. After all, even if it doesn't give you the hability to grab ghosts, without it you shouldn't be able to suck Essence, even if you could grab a ghost. I second the oppinion that UA should eliminate or aleviate the drawbacks of such blood, but it's main purpose is to give it the capacity to nourish you as vampiric blood. You know, not just to broaden your feeding options at BP 6+, but so those other options don't risk a Vinculum.<br /> <br /> That said, I would mostly use a simple system of give the vampire a Condition based on each type of blood. Nothing very complicated, just a &quot;do this to resolve the Condition&quot; will do. You can give the players a drawback that is also a boon with this, in a simple way. The beats from those will be enough to make most supernatural blood addicting in its own way, and those beats can be used precisely to explain the power of this strange blood, if you interpret the traits bought with such experience as being spontaneous manifestations born from inhuman Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:14:41-07:00","id":579303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579142#post579142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! That just gave me an idea! What if the weird effects like the Frenzy penalty from werewolf blood and the hallucinations from changeling blood only happen if the vampire doesn't have Unnatural Affinity? Those drawbacks come from not being acclimatized to their unusual vitae, but with the Merit those side effects go away.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the side effects. Considering the power inherent in these other beings, taking their blood and internalizing it in their Beast furnace should have some effect.<br /> <br /> But I'd also prefer something for werewolves consuming the flesh of others, as there is a similar refinery at work but so far only changelings and fetches really have any difference as far as I know.<br /> <br /> You are what you eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:20:43-07:00","id":579335,"title":"","content":"Unnatural Affinity always comes up in these threads. It was apparently intended for Blood Potency 6+ Kindred to have other options, but the merit itself is worded openly enough to be usable by anyone for &quot;odd&quot; things like ghosts or Purified or whatever normally doesn't give Vitae.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:40:47-07:00","id":579406,"title":"","content":"I know, I just like the idea of Unnatural Affinity also removing negative side effects of certain supernatural blood sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T04:41:41-07:00","id":579720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=578919#post578919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it necessarily needs to be bad for the vampire. The 1e effects of Werewolf blood, for example, is a mixed blessing any way you look at it. I just like the idea of supernatural creatures' blood having special effects, but those effects dont all need to be bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Generally speaking, most people asssume it is. While werewolf can be considered a mixed blessing, the bad seems to outweigh the good by a fair amount - its playing with fire. Meanwhile, mage blood causes hallucinations, no benefit. Changeling blood was addictive drug-like messing with perception, no benefit, promethean was just nasty. And so on. There's definitely a theme of &quot;non-human blood is bad!&quot; as the game goes on.<br /> <br /> You might protest that it might not be bad, but looking through the thread? All that anyone suggested (beyond the Unnatural Affinity feeding thing) is negative effects\u200b. &quot;Supernatural blood is bad!&quot; is absolutely the message I'm taking away from the discussion here.<br /> <br /> And I still argue that its generally detrimental to games. While there are plots and stories where having it be bad is definitely worthwhile, I find that having more benefit than detriment serves as a kind of plot hook that encourages more stories, seeking out rare and exotic blood. Blood is everything to the Kindred. Side effects are one thing, they could even be a good thing. But the overwhelming number of so-called side effects are overwhelmingly negative.<br /> <br /> Lets put it this way. What storyhooks does having all these negative effects bring? How does it encourage stories? Having vampires that are interested in other supers for their blood can lead to tension and conflict as others supers look askance at the idea of being fed from. How does having negative effects encourage stories? Because that's the bottom line - we're here to tell stories, so what stories come from this?<br /> <br /> Also, if we're going to do this, we should do it in the form of Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579134#post579134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need Unnatural Affinity for this. Interestingly, by RAW it looks like you need a merit to get nourishment at all from other supernaturals in 2e. The first sentence of Unnatural Affinity seems to say such, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Blood Potency section that discusses the merit indicates that we're talking about BP+ elders, so taken in context, I'd say its regular feeding time without the merit. As if human, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:02:30-07:00","id":579726,"title":"","content":"I think the plot idea behind making the effects of supernatural blood generally not good had to do with setting up exceptions as the plot.<br /> <br /> So the cons might outweigh the pros, unless you...<ul><li>perform the Blood Sorcery Ritual</li> <li>Learn the Devotion</li> <li>Buy the Merit</li> <li>Learn the Coil</li> <li>Perform the Scale</li> <li>Do the Misc. Ritual thing</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Making it a situation where NPCs or PCs invest in the idea to gain the possibility, creating a sort of resource that might engender the interest or hostility of other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:47:25-07:00","id":579734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579132#post579132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit better than just that though, yes it's just vitae, but functionaly equivalent to vampire vitae for feeding restriction whitout any of the risks of vinculum.<br /> That seems like a good benefit on it's own already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Anything beyond what's in the V:tR 2e corebook, though, is probably going to remain 'just Vitae'. This came up in a dev discussion recently when we were mulling over whether werewolf blood in 2e gave any special effects for vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:42:31-07:00","id":580431,"title":"","content":"In my games, contrary to what a lot of other people are saying, a vampire drinking from a mummy would puke it up violently, seeing as Sekhem is basically made up of pure life energy, and vampires are totally undead. The concept here is a bit like the &quot;Wafer Thin Mint&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> <b>Warning: Gross but funny Monty Python bit</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lhbHTjMLN5c\" data-code=\"lhbHTjMLN5c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lhbHTjMLN5c/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:31:59-07:00","id":580930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=579726#post579726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the plot idea behind making the effects of supernatural blood generally not good had to do with setting up exceptions as the plot.<br /> <br /> So the cons might outweigh the pros, unless you......<br /> Making it a situation where NPCs or PCs invest in the idea to gain the possibility, creating a sort of resource that might engender the interest or hostility of other characters.</div> </div> </div> </div> But why go through all the trouble in the first place? What's the pay out? So far, there isn't one except werewolves, and that's a debatable benefit when you can easily feed with no one the wiser with level 1 Disciplines or Lashing Out. <br /> <br /> Why should someone go through that &quot;find the exception&quot; plot in the first place? That's the part I'm stuck on. I mean, the werewolf drawback is easily ignored if we talk about bringing Coils into play, but why should we worry about the setup in the first place? Why should the average vamp player care or be interested in such stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:00:14-07:00","id":580951,"title":"","content":"They're not supposed to be rewards. Most supernaturals aren't identifiable, a vampire can't tell a mage from a changeling from a sin-eater without putting some extra work into it. So in the course of their feeding they're likely to bite into one and get some weird effects.<br /> <br /> It's a plot hook.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, in a crossover game or a game where a vampire is aligned closely with another kind of supernatural, they may show tendencies that reveal that closeness. A gangrel who's part of a werewolf pack is more prone to frenzy, a daeva who's befriended changelings seems wide-eyed and tripping a lot of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:16:26-07:00","id":580965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=580951#post580951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not supposed to be rewards. Most supernaturals aren't identifiable, a vampire can't tell a mage from a changeling from a sin-eater without putting some extra work into it. So in the course of their feeding they're likely to bite into one and get some weird effects<br /> <br /> It's a plot hook..</div> </div> </div> </div> That can be done without making it negative. If anything, the negative discourages further interaction with said plot hook. Strange tasting blood is fine; you can have strange effects without it being a penalty. There's no reason for it to be a negative effect. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, in a crossover game or a game where a vampire is aligned closely with another kind of supernatural, they may show tendencies that reveal that closeness. A gangrel who's part of a werewolf pack is more prone to frenzy, a daeva who's befriended changelings seems wide-eyed and tripping a lot of the time. </div> </div> </div> Putting aside that the Ven are the ones who resonate more with changelings, like the gangrel and wolves, and that those two clans are already known for being a bit crazy and frenzy prone... <br /> <br /> Why would a PC player be interested in that? That's what it comes down to. NPCs can act however the ST wants them to. It should be something that the PCs get involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:00:50-07:00","id":581120,"title":"","content":"I'd expect that without &quot;Unnatural Affinity&quot; a vampire wouldn't be able to take sustenance from any other supernatural if their blood potency was above 2. When it comes to creating vitae vampires are like Spirits which can only derive essence from a matching resonance. As their own resonance (blood potency) grows further from the human norm, it becomes harder to find a match. At first any living blood will do, but over time they need human, and finally vampire blood, to gain nourishment. As other supernaturals are differentiated from humans, in ways far different from vampires, I'd treat their blood like animal blood. It's only close enough to feed from when the vampire is closest to human.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of supernatural blood bringing some benefits though. When a vampire drinks from another vampire it helps them learn that vampire's disciplines, so I'd treat other supernaturals the same way. A vampire who feeds from a werewolf might gain insight needed to learn Protean, or a Mind mage might awaken the powers of Animalism, Dominate, or Majesty in vampire by feeding him and trying to teach him magic. Perhaps a local branch of the Ordo Dracul might consider a diet of werewolf blood as essential to developing the coils of the Mystery of the Wyrm. Also, new Mysteries of the Dragon, Cruac rites, Devotions, or Disciplines, might result from feeding on other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:33:01-07:00","id":581832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=580965#post580965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That can be done without making it negative. If anything, the negative discourages further interaction with said plot hook. Strange tasting blood is fine; you can have strange effects without it being a penalty. There's no reason for it to be a negative effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason for it to be a positive one. An affect is all you need, and none of the penalties are that bad. Plus they get Vitae from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would a PC player be interested in that? That's what it comes down to. NPCs can act however the ST wants them to. It should be something that the PCs get involved. </div> </div> </div>Because a player likes another game and wants their character to act like a character from it, or close to a character from it. That's why there's a Dead Wolves bloodline to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-06-2015, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T22:02:25-07:00","id":581941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=578251#post578251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Werewolf blood was worth 2.5 Vitae per &quot;point&quot; worth of blood taken and imposed a -2 penalty to resist Frenzy for a number of nights equal to twice the number of blood points (not Vitae) taken. Mage blood was worth the normal amount of Vitae and caused a Derangement for a number of nights equal to the amount of Vitae taken. Changeling blood was worth the normal amount of Vitae and imposed a -X penalty to perception rolls for one night, where X is the amount of Vitae taken. Promethean blood was worth 1/2 a point of Vitae per &quot;point&quot; of blood taken and had no additional effects. I believe those were the only ones that had &quot;official&quot; special effects in 1e. I've been poking around with updating those to mechanics that fit a bit better with 2e design, and considering adding some effects to the other splats, but I haven't gotten a ton done on it yet. If you like I'll push it up on my conversion to-do list and post the results in a couple days.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's assuming the Promethean in question has blood...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:48:22-07:00","id":583181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=581941#post581941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's assuming the Promethean in question has blood...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all Prometheans have a fluid with similar function, and Galateids have that Sanguine humour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T23:52:02-07:00","id":583240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=583181#post583181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, all Prometheans have a fluid with similar function, and Galateids have that Sanguine humour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I'm just picturing the look on a vampire's face when he bites into an Osiron, and gets a mouth full of phlegm!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T01:55:03-07:00","id":583284,"title":"","content":"Ewwwwwwwww!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T06:14:15-07:00","id":583420,"title":"","content":"Werewolves, mages, changelings, and Prometheans all have canon answers to some degree (which have been given). My headcanons for the others are:<br /> <br /> <b>Sineaters:</b> Similar to werewolves; the vampire gets twice the normal vitae (additionally, each health level the Sineater loses costs her a point of plasm, as some of it is in the blood), but the vampire gets a -2 to resist Rotschreck for a number of nights equal to their vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummies:</b> If the mummy doesn't have a Sahu going, nothing happens at all. No blood, no vitae, no Kiss, no ill effects. A vampire needs the wherewithal to feed on ghosts in order to feed on a mummy with Sahu, but if they do, it's Christmas: the vitae they drink is multiplied by half the mummy's current Sekhem (round up), and is not limited by their normal maximum pool - on the downside, if they do drink more vitae than they can normally hold, they are drawn to the mummy's first and final purpose until it drops to within their pool size.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge:</b> Normal vitae, but it tastes fiery; the Beast twitches when they taste it, but not enough to require Rotschreck.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b> Normal vitae, but tastes a bit on the icky side.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts:</b> If the Beast is Sated or Starving, the vampire gets twice the Vitae (either the fullness of the keenness is good). If the Beast is Starving or Ravenous, her Hunger infects the Beast of the vampire - for 1 night per vitae, the vampire's Beast craves satisfaction through the Begotten's Hunger instead of blood - the vampire still <i>needs</i> blood (and doesn't need to satisfy the Hunger to survive), only what might trigger Wassail is affected. Needless to say, this can be a weird experience, but some vampires like it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:42:18-07:00","id":583546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=581832#post581832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason for it to be a positive one. An affect is all you need, and none of the penalties are that bad. Plus they get Vitae from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's moving the goalpost. I never said it had to be positive. Could be mixed blessing, could be positive, could be <br /> <br /> <i>The overwhelming majority are negative effects. Why? What stories does that bring that anything else wouldn't?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because a player likes another game and wants their character to act like a character from it, or close to a character from it. That's why there's a Dead Wolves bloodline to begin with. </div> </div> </div> Getting penatlies from drinking that blood helps play that style... how? I can play a mage-type using Mehket and joining one of the mystical covenants. Werewolf? A CotC gangrel with either low Resolve+Composure, or high and a fondness for riding the wave. A changeling-like being who's been abused, has trouble relating to humanity (thus, Lost), enjoys playing court, makes supernatural pacts, and a touch of madness? Ventrue Invictus, at your service. Anarchist professional liar spy that infiltrates others and fights the establishment? Carthian Daeva. <br /> <br /> Drinking the blood is not necessary for that kind of concept... the penalties and negative effects do not lend themselves to playing the style either! Werewolves are all about the shapeshifting and the hunt, not mindless rage. Mages are about investigating mysteries, not hallucinations. The blood drinking changes nothing. Also, remember that Dead Wolves bloodline was the result of embracing a wolf blooded, not drinking werewolf blood, so justification. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:32:00-07:00","id":583583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=583546#post583546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are about investigating mysteries, not hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying about the Werewolf blood, but this is a misunderstanding of what the hallucinations that result from drinking Mage Blood are. They're implied to basically be Mage Sight, which overlays all that Supernal symbolism over everything. To a vampire with no appreciation of what these things mean, it looks like complete, hallucinatory nonsense. I'm sure you could create an NPC or a merit or a Bloodline or whatever who might be able to make something more useful out of the overwhelming sensory detail of symbol truths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:57:24-07:00","id":583635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats?p=583546#post583546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's moving the goalpost. I never said it had to be positive. Could be mixed blessing, could be positive, could be</div> </div> </div> </div>It's following the conversation. You said they don't have to be a negative one, I said they don't have to be a positive one. They already are a mixed blessing, because you get Vitae from it, which is a gain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Getting penatlies from drinking that blood helps play that style... how? </div> </div> </div>The same way taking dramatic failures for beats helps, because you're playing a character who screws up badly. The same way persistent, negative conditions help, because you're playing out the, again, minor penalty of your actions and life. The same way flaws help, because you're playing a character with a disadvantage. And in all of these you have the mechanical disadvantage to back it up, and the rewards for following through with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-08-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:08:02-07:00","id":585550,"title":"","content":"Surely, the effects doesn't have to be allways negative. I agree with that.<br /> <br /> But my point is: if there should be OFFICIAL effects, they shouldn't be positive EITHER.<br /> <br /> You can't reason your point just thinking from the Vampire perspective, because any official statement affects the whole WoD, including crossover chronicles. And I'm not talking about cross with splat NPCs in a all-Vamps PCs chronicle.<br /> <br /> If any official response gives mechanical benefits to this blood, this WILL become an issue in a game where the PCs can be of various splats. That is the problem. It is just a feature in an all-Vamps game, and a reason for Vamps to look-out for Others. But when you can have a Vamp and an Other on the same group, this is the road to powerplay. CAN work, but won't work allways.<br /> <br /> That's why I think those effects should be handled by ST, not by official rules. And if anything official is to be said, them I do prefer negative effects than positive ones. They have a lesser impact when you make a decision that WILL impact everyone. I like, indeed, that 2e didn't made any statement until now, just Unnatural Affinity.<br /> <br /> A simple default for everything with rules to use Conditions to make your own effects (for good or ill) would be just perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:05:41-07:00","id":593456,"title":"","content":"I tend to like expanding the effects of what the blood of other supernaturals does to give a more concrete benefit in addition to the drawback, making it a very mixed blessing. Taking into account 2e rules, I'd do something like:<br /> <br /> Werewolves: 2 Vitae per lethal, -1 to frenzy rolls for a night per -vitae- gained, but increase your effective BP for the sake of bonuses in frenzy (only) by 1 during that time.<br /> <br /> Mages: You have access to the active mage sight of the mage you've taken vitae from for an hour per lethal caused. But that includes the penalties it causes, and you can't turn it off through any means, and it still taxes your willpower for each of those hours despite not being able to shut it down (if you run out, it doesn't stop early, either). Might also impose a condition related to the mage sight if you weren't expecting it.<br /> <br /> Changelings: Will depend on 2e mechanics, but the perception penalty still applies for the night (-1 per vitae taken). On the bright side, you can see through the mask for the duration, too... if you can figure out what's a changeling and what's a hallucination superimposed on a normal person.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: The blood of Sin-Eaters brings the Vampire that much closer to their undead side. Utilizing vitae to mimic life costs 1 extra vitae for 1 night per lethal caused. On the bright side, you gain access to the SIn-Eater's death sight abilities, and if you have a way to feed on ghosts, through a merit, gift, or discipline, you gain 2 vitae per lethal done to the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Mummies: I don't like Mummies. Do whatever.<br /> <br /> Demons: You get no Vitae from a Demon if they don't have a Cover active, though it causes damage and otherwise as normal. If they do have a cover up, you feed from them normally. Nothing too special here; any specific effects that could become recognizable make little sense given the ability of cover to spoof and similar.<br /> <br /> Beasts: The Vampire's feeding habits become tainted by the Hunger of the Beast. For one night per lethal caused to the Beast, the Kindred needs to spend a willpower to gain vitae from a source that doesn't at least peripherally align with that beast's hunger. On the bright side, when it DOES align, you gain double Vitae, and that includes every vitae after the first taken from the Beast themself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}